    "stop_reason": "success",
    "result_text": "The full test suite passes (BUILD SUCCESS, 0 failures/errors).\n\nI implemented the city-capacity rule following the project's OfficeFloor function-injection conventions:\n\n1. **`CheckOwnerCityCapacity`** (`rest/function/owner/`) \u2014 a new pipeline step that counts existing owners in the request's city (case-insensitively, matching `AssignCustomerCode`) and throws when the count is \u2265 50.\n2. **`OwnerCityFullException`** (`rest/escalation/`) \u2014 a checked exception carrying the full city.\n3. **`OwnerCityFullExceptionHandler`** \u2014 responds `409 CONFLICT`, mirroring the existing duplicate-owner handlers.\n4. **`org.springframework.samples.petclinic.rest.escalation.OwnerCityFullException.yml`** \u2014 wires the exception to its handler.\n5. **`owners.POST.yml`** \u2014 inserted the `checkCityCapacity` step (under `transaction` governance) after the household-uniqueness check and before `build`, so a full city is rejected before any record is persisted.\n\nThe check runs after `ValidateNewOwner` publishes the request (which already guarantees a non-blank city) and before `BuildOwner`, consistent with the other pre-build guard steps.",
